{"availability":"available","full":"Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen","name":"vuegen","description":"VueGen automates the creation of reports from bioinformatics outputs, supporting formats like PDF, HTML, DOCX, ODT, PPTX, Reveal.js, Jupyter notebooks, and Streamlit web applications. Users simply provide a directory with output files and VueGen compiles them into a structured report.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":40,"forks":0,"created":"2023-06-13T09:09:35Z","updated":"2026-09-23T12:48:52Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://vuegen.readthedocs.io","topics":["bioinformatics-software","data-visualization","developer-tools","python","quarto","reports","streamlit"],"demo":"https://earth-microbiome-vuegen-demo.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.059Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.059Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.059Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.059Z","stars":40,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["VueGen is a Python package that automates the creation of scientific reports.","VueGen is a tool that automates the creation of reports from bioinformatics outputs, allowing researchers with minimal coding experience to communicate their results effectively. With VueGen, users can produce reports by simply specifying a directory containing output files, such as plots, tables, networks, Markdown text, HTML components, and API calls, along with the report format. Supported formats include documents (PDF, HTML, DOCX, ODT), presentations (PPTX, Reveal.js), Jupyter notebooks, and Streamlit web applications.","A YAML configuration file is generated from the directory to define the structure of the report. Users can customize the report by modifying the configuration file, or they can create their own configuration file instead of passing a directory as input. The configuration file specifies the structure of the report, including sections, subsections, and various components such as plots, dataframes, markdown, html, and API calls."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ce2c122af790c5a71b6eef3553d23ddd9c707073710871d6fea24d8e16fc9d7","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.190Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.190Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"VueGen is a Python package that automates the creation of scientific reports.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Failing examples are more than welcome via GitHub issues (you need a GitHub account).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5ce2c122af790c5a71b6eef3553d23ddd9c707073710871d6fea24d8e16fc9d7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.191Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T12:48:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Multiomics-Analytics-Group/vuegen/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:57.192Z","hash":"5ce2c122af790c5a71b6eef3553d23ddd9c707073710871d6fea24d8e16fc9d7","originalBytes":31608,"storedBytes":31608,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["vuegen","file","directory","report","streamlit","example","configuration","gui","available","bash","data","colab","install","conda","docs","quarto","run","using","component","demo","html","python","case","docker","earth","files","folder","microbiome","nextflow","config","create","nf-core","type","command","emp","following","github","package","plots","repository","such","description.md","environment","license","link","note","pip","project","running","users","components","here","installation","installed","issues","jupyter","module","need","note